      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "One of the solutions i tought of was to make the avatar local but visible if the remote user has the same avatar saved on their avatars folder. \n\nso like having a test avatar that can be seen by other users if they have the same one on their local files too. \n\nIt seems like a tedious process but could be a nice feature if you want to be 99% sure that the avatar won't be downloaded by an unwanted person",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "64588a4f05aa6b08fe214d88",
      "author": {
        "_id": "621afb77c20d153ae60791a9",
        "alias": "Selected Giraffe",
        "aliasID": "65c2a20bed6eefce4c60c21e",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/0d5b7e89f87a8f70d1a303289c9333a2.png",
        "created": "2022-02-27T04:17:59.309Z",
        "name": "Litе",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-05-08T05:36:15.320Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "644da1c91512040901b55a1f",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "My controversial opinion, would just be an unnecessary band-aid solution to an issue which tbh barely affects the majority of the player base. \n\nFeel free to debate me on this but coming from someone who makes custom models and avatars I feel this fear is a bit irrational as only a very small minority of players are interested in avatar theft to begin with. I understand the fear of having your hard work ripped off trust me. But for most it simply isn't worth the effort to reverse engineer an avatar and use it as their own, and even if they do you can just get it taken down assuming you own the avatar. \n\nBest way I've found to mitigate this problem entirely is just making my avis public, even my favorites. Isn't at all worth the effort getting a public avatar when you can just use it in its entirety from the get go.\n\nUltimately this problem does have a lot of layers to it and different perspectives. What I normally tell people who wanna make avatars is to treat them like Minecraft skins. You're making the decision to put your work out in the world when you upload an avatar.\n\nBetter solution to this specific problem imo would be just encrypting the files but that would increase load times and even then smart players would work around it in no time. Truth be told there really isn't a perfect solution. So I've just stopped caring that much instead just focusing on the joy of creation and sharing that creation.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "64681205f5f42c092441fe9b",
      "author": {
        "_id": "62def0766bc855559c02818a",
        "alias": "Curved Koi",
        "aliasID": "65c4ffd6ed6eefce4cc0989a",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/fba75060993cfcbc9dfff9b30f462823.png",
        "created": "2022-07-25T19:35:18.442Z",
        "name": "SheepyCakes",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-05-20T00:19:17.126Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
