      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "644da1c91512040901b55a1f",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So, I'm going to tell you why this isn't possible. \n\nWhen you load into a VRChat world, the game has to load your avatar cache. The cache of your avatar is how people are ripping/stealing it, but regardless of whether people are able to view your avatar, the cache of the avatar you are wearing is the folder that will load into the cache of the world both you and the other player are inhabiting. There is nothing you can do to prevent this. This is a feature of the unity engine VRChat utilizes. The reason your cache folder in VRChat constantly fills up and you have to empty it is because you're visiting a lot of worlds and a lot of people's avatars are occupying those worlds. Regardless of what you do, your avatar will be up for grabs by rippers if you are wearing it in a public space.\n\nThe only solution is to not wear an avatar you care about being stolen in a public world.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
