  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "One of the biggest concerns for VRChat users is the potential for their avatar's vrca's to be downloaded and manipulated by malicious users. While there have been attempts to mitigate this issue, most protection measures come to a common issue, the vrca always require the files to be loaded onto the malicious user's PC, making it vulnerable to theft.\n\nI propose a new feature that would give users more control over who can see their avatars. With Avatar Visibility Control, users can choose to only show their avatars to trusted users, friends, or a specific group of people based on VRChat's ranking system. This feature would mitigate their avatar's vrca's from being downloaded and manipulated by malicious users.\n\nBy implementing Avatar Visibility Control, VRChat can provide a more secure environment for its users to create and use avatars without fear of theft. This feature will encourage more users to use their avatars in public lobbies, leading to a more engaging community.\n\nLet's take a step forward in protecting users' avatars by giving them the ability to control who can see and access them.",
